# The reviewer's key, wherever it lands. TCC starts the Advisor from the PROJECT folder and the
# method reads `.critic-env` from several places, so one can appear in a working tree that is also
# this repository — which is public. Ignored by NAME rather than by path, because the method looks
# in `./`, `./scripts/` and the project mirror, and a rule tied to one of them is a rule that
# misses the other two (SKL-023, HUB-025). Held by `test_packaging.py`, which asks git rather than
# reading this file.
.critic-env
critic-env
